A||||2||wkayl||Another deep poem (by my daughter)...||||1||
Z||000000||wkayl||12-05-2000||10:14 PM||||My daughter wrote this after The Columbine shooting.  She was 13 at the time...<P>I have this anger<BR>That I want to show<BR>Toward two young men<BR>I don't even know.<P>They showed up at<BR>School one day<BR>Shooting anything that<BR>Stood in their way.<P>No reason or motive<BR>Just anger and hate<BR>And the number of injured<BR>Increasing with a fast rate.<P>Students and teachers<BR>Yelling in fear<BR>The killers so close<BR>People on phones could hear.<P>I don't know how that feels<BR>And I hope I never will<BR>I don't want to die for<BR>Someone's moment of thrill.<P>I think there was something wrong<BR>With Eric Harris' head<BR>He killed 13 people and<BR>Now he too is dead.<P>Dylan Klebold was the other gunman <BR>On a rampage that day<BR>Teachers say he had great talent<BR>But it was Eric that stood in his way.<P>No one knows what God will decide,<BR>It is very hard to tell<BR>I hope that they repented<BR>And they won't go to hell.<P>To all the victims that were killed on April 20, 1999 at<BR>Columbine High School, <BR>I will see you in heaven.<P>All my love,<BR>Dnyee'||||reg||1
Z||000001||hugh||12-05-2000||10:43 PM||||Very nicely written,by someone with a very pretty name.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||12-06-2000||07:58 AM||||Vey Nice. I have friend that had gone to that school a few years prior to that event. It shook him to the core.||||reg||14
